RF.put("questb:b21",{"8661":{"id":8661,"t":"Doomcaller's Robes","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nHusk of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Night Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nDoomcaller's Robes\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warlock Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8661\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Doomcaller's Robes this quest\nBring the the Husk of the Old God, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8581":{"id":8581,"t":"The Horde Needs More Firebloom!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Firebloom to Batrider Pele'keiki at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Firebloom Firebloom , Sha'ni Proudtusk 18.2 % , Alexia Ironknife 12.5 % , Treant Spirit 3.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Pele'keiki know you come to help. Bring many firebloom and make him very happy. Pele'keiki might make big bombs with firebloom. Drop them on insects from his bat over Ahn'Qiraj when war come. But Pele'keiki need more firebloom, ‹class›!\nYou gonna bring Pele'keiki that firebloom, real quick now. Come back with at least as much as last time, and Pele'keiki be pleased.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"This no joke, ‹class›? You bring Pele'keiki firebloom that fast? Pele'keiki count them up right now, mon! You makin' Pele'keiki so happy, he be tellin' everyone, ‹name› best firebloom collector ever! Pele'keiki can't wait for war to start. Now we really light up the sky over Silithus, right, bruddah?!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33.4,"y":69.3,"n":"Batrider Pele'keiki","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7301":{"id":7301,"t":"Fallen Sky Lords","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Frostwolf territory and search for Wing Commander Slidore, Wing Commander Vipore, and Wing Commander Ichman. Return to Commander Duffy should you complete your mission.\nIchman's Location Discovered\nVipore's Location Discovered\nSlidore's Location Discovered","desc":"We got them held prisoner, ‹race›. I'm talking about their Wing Commanders. It was a furious battle in the skies but they finally fell! Unfortunately, our best pilots were shot down in a counterattack against Frostwolf Keep. You gotta find out what happened to them.\nSearch Tower Point West and Frostwolf Keep. These were their last known locations. Search these areas thoroughly.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Anything I would care to hear?","done":"Unbelievable! You did free them, right? Right??? Well at the very least we know where they were held.\nStart Commander Duffy Alterac Valley End Commander Duffy Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7301","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6901":{"id":6901,"t":"Launch the Attack!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Assault Orders","done":"It's about time! Now we can show the Alliance their folly in coming to Alterac Valley!\nStart Warmaster Garrick End Warmaster Garrick Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6901","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6741":{"id":6741,"t":"More Booty!","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Armor Scraps Winterax Warrior 80 % , Winterax Mystic 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % and 4 more","back":"I need more armor scraps, ‹name›! Do you have any?","done":"Thanks again, ‹name›. You do the Horde proud...\nStart Smith Regzar Alterac Valley End Smith Regzar Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6741\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Enemy Booty\nBring 20 Armor Scraps to Smith Regzar in Frostwolf Village.\nSmith Regzar Alterac Valley\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] More Booty! this quest\nSmith Regzar Alterac Valley","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7221":{"id":7221,"t":"Speak with Prospector Stonehewer","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Prospector Stonehewer in the Dun Baldar garrison.","desc":"Ah, ‹name›, reporting for duty are you? Great, the Stormpikes can use everyone we can muster!\nSpeak with Prospector Stonehewer in Dun Baldar. She's recruiting for a vital mission into enemy territory. You'll find Stonehewer in the bottom of the Dun Baldar garrison.\nAnd keep an eye out as you go through Dun Baldar. There's plenty to do for a hardworking ‹class› who's not afraid to get his/her hands dirty.","rew":"Experience: 650","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":40.7,"y":79.6,"n":"Prospector Stonehewer","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7141":{"id":7141,"t":"The Battle of Alterac","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 70s instead of 0.","obj":"Enter Alterac Valley, defeat the Horde general Drek'thar, and then return to Prospector Stonehewer in the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"The Explorers' League believes there are artifacts in Alterac Valley, but the Frostwolf orcs won't let us explore. We can't allow the Horde to stop our scholarly pursuits! Defeat the Frostwolf general, Drek'Thar. With him dead, the orcs will lose their edge.\nDrek'Thar is in Frostwolf Keep, in the south of Alterac Valley. Vanquish him, and then return to me.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Go, ‹name›. Go to Alterac Valley and defeat the orc general!","done":"Well done, ‹name›! With the Horde's nose bloodied after the death of their general, we'll have the breathing room we need to explore!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":40.7,"y":79.6,"n":"Prospector Stonehewer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8261":{"id":8261,"t":"Arathor Standard Care Package","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArathor Standard Care Package\nExperience: 380\n+10 reputation with The League of Arathor","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46,"y":45.2,"n":"Samuel Hawke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"6581":{"id":6581,"t":"Warsong Saw Blades","lv":27,"min":22,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deadly Blunderbuss","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Saw Blades","back":"Direct from Ratchet, the Warsong saw blades! Yep, I have them right here.\n..But what sort of payment do you have for me? You can't just take them, you know! My time isn't cheap!\nWhat I really need is a good gun to carry with me on my travels. A girl's gotta protect herself, you know? There's a gun I really like that I'm sure an engineer would have no problem making.\nSo, if you bring me a deadly blunderbuss, I'll give you the saw blade shipment. Do we have a deal?","done":"This is perfect -- just the thing! Well, here's the shipment.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.1,"y":61.5,"n":"Pixel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"4581":{"id":4581,"t":"Kayneth Stillwind","lv":29,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Shindrell's Note to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.\nShindrell's Note\nProvided: Shindrell's Note","desc":"The druid Kayneth Stillwind sent word to me. He would like a report of the happenings along our coast and in the forests surrounding Astranaar. He fears there is a corruption moving through Ashenvale... and he may be right.\nHere, take my report to him. You will find him in the shrine of Forest Song, in the Nightsong Woods to the east.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you have something for me?","done":"Ah, Shindrell's report! Many thanks, ‹name›. Shindrell is a fine sentinel, brave and keen. I must read this for clues of a wickedness I fear is moving through Ashenvale.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.7,"y":48.8,"n":"Shindrell Swiftfire","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":85.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Kayneth Stillwind","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3381":{"id":3381,"t":"A meeting with the master","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 2 Undamaged Hippogryph Feathers to Sanath Lim-yo in Azshara if you wish to speak to his master.\n2 Undamaged Hippogryph Feather","desc":"Ah, a young ‹race› come to speak to Sanath. What a wonderful day! I am so honored to have you grace me with your presence. Thank you!\nPlease... do not be so arrogant to assume my sarcasm was a compliment. Let us get one thing straight: I don't like you. But this little conversation doesn't have anything to do with us--it has to do with my master.\nBring me a couple hippogryph feathers for my arrows and I'll give you leave to see him. He's asked that I send adventurers to him if they proved worthy enough.\nLevel 48 , requires level 45 Difficulty 45 46 51 60 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 3381","cats":["azshara"]},"3541":{"id":3541,"t":"Delivery to Jes'rimon","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tablet of Jin'yael to Jes'rimon in Orgrimmar.\nTablet of Jin'yael Tablet of Jin'yael\nProvided: Tablet of Jin'yael","desc":"I have a fence in Orgrimmar. He resides in The Drag. He's difficult to nail down if you don't know where to look, but if you go looking in one of the highest buildings there you should have no problem finding him.\nDo me a favor though, don't go shouting to all of Kalimdor that he's there and what his business is--it'd be bad for both of us.\nHe'll give us more than a fair price for the Tablet of Jin'yael. I'm not sure why, but you should have seen how excited he was to hear about its whereabouts.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550","back":"Yes, what you be needin', mon? I got many tings to be takin' care of today, and you not be on me agenda as one of them. Pester me, and I make sure that changes.","done":"Ahhh, Jediga be sendin' her package all the way from Azshara. Good. I be waitin' on this.\nJediga, now that be a fine woman... deadly too. What could be better?\nLook at this... the tablet be in perfect condition. You make a good messenger, ‹name›.\nAzshara Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":55.5,"y":34.1,"n":"Jes'rimon","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"3141":{"id":3141,"t":"Loramus","lv":57,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to Loramus Thalipedes tell his story.","desc":"So you wish to battle demons? You would do well to listen to my tale.","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"Do not interrupt me, ‹race›.","done":"So be it...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"3621":{"id":3621,"t":"The Formation of Felbane","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Shipment to Galvan the Ancient in Stranglethorn Vale.\nShipment to Galvan\nProvided: Shipment to Galvan","desc":"The weapons are ready to be forged. You must take the tempered azsharite to one with the ability to harness fel energy.\nIn Stranglethorn Vale such a blacksmith exists. Galvan the Ancient, leader of the Mithril Order, will craft the weapons to your specifications. You will find his encampment between Zul'Gurub and the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound.\nMay your determination and faith carry you through this ordeal. Should you fail, know that your God smiles down upon you, mortal.","rew":"Experience: 4,650","back":"Loramus, eh? It has been many years since I have heard that name.","done":"My goodness, I can only imagine what you went through to get these materials. Few venture into Azshara and return alive, let alone those that face demi-gods and giants!\nAzshara Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"6821":{"id":6821,"t":"Eye of the Emberseer","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 56.","obj":"Bring the Eye of the Emberseer to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\nEye of the Emberseer Pyroguard Emberseer","desc":"You have shown me that you can defeat our enemies and perform missions to further the cause of the Waterlords. But until now you have only faced lesser foes... if pitted against a powerful enemy, can you prevail?\nThat is your new task.\nHigh up in Blackrock Spire the orcs have captured a servant of fire, the Pyroguard Emberseer. Find his place of imprisonment, slay his captors, and then slay the emberseer. Bring me his eye and it will show me your worth.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Do you have the Eye, ‹class›? Do you have the strength to enter Blackrock Spire?","done":"Ah, so you do have the strength. And you have the cunning as well, for Blackrock Spire is more than a match for brute strength alone.\nIndeed ‹name›, you may yet prove a valued ally to us...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4341":{"id":4341,"t":"Kharan Mighthammer","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,400 experience instead of 5,800, 1.1 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and find Kharan Mighthammer.\nThe King mentioned that Kharan was being held prisoner there - perhaps you should try looking for a prison.","desc":"You have been to the smoldering ruins of Thaurissan? Did you happen to run into a pitiful lout named Kharan Mighthammer? The dwarf that was supposedly watching over my baby girl!\n<The King sobs.>\nAnd now she's gone, ‹name›!\nI have had my men turn the Steppes upside down. The only clue they have as to the whereabouts of my daughter is that she may be inside the Depths. For all I know, she could be dead!\nKharan is supposedly being held prisoner there... find him! I want answers!","rew":"Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Please, let me explain.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4981":{"id":4981,"t":"Operative Bijou","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and find out what happened to Bijou.","desc":"Never trust a goblin. That's what it comes down to, ‹name›.\nBijou is her name - one of our slipperiest operatives. I found out she was working for some shady exotic pet dealer out of the Burning Steppes named Kibler, in essence, two timing us. Worse yet, she was using Horde funds to finance her operations.\nI want her brought back here alive.\nShe was last seen entering Blackrock Spire. Find her and bring her back.\nAnd ‹name›, do not let her sweet talk you.","rew":"Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"I won't lie to you, ‹race›. I needed the money! Kibler pays very, very well - much better than the K.E.F. ever could.\nBut don't doubt my loyalties! Why do you think I'm down here? To get that crazy goblin some exotic animal eggs or something equally inane? No, only someone truly daft would come to Blackrock Spire to collect pets. Yep, I don't reckon too many people like that exist in this world.\n<Bijou laughs.>\nThe last thing we need are those kinds of people breeding.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.9,"y":47.6,"n":"Lexlort","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5301":{"id":5301,"t":"The Art of the Armorsmith","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To become an armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Okothos: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.\n4 Ornate Mithril Helm\n2 Ornate Mithril Boots\nOrnate Mithril Breastplate","desc":"Satisfaction. It is what I draw from the hammer and the anvil. To see a proud Horde warrior protected under my steel reminds me of what it is to be alive. It is an addiction that I dare never give up, ‹name›.\nI can not grant you this satisfaction, merely set you upon the path. As with all of life's endeavors, the path of the armorsmith is a journey.\nIf you wish to be one of the select few, you need only to ask and I shall train, but, a task you must first complete.","rew":"You will learn: Armorsmith\nExperience: 3,150","back":"I will pound the steel until the breath itself has been taken from me.","done":"This is the final step before you begin your new career as an armorsmith, ‹name›. Should you choose to back out, now would be your last chance. Otherwise, prepare yourself for a lifetime of glory.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.8,"y":24.1,"n":"Okothos Ironrager","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2581":{"id":2581,"t":"Snickerfang Jowls","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Snickerfang Jowls, two Blasted Boar Lungs, and one Scorpok Pincer to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Snickerfang Jowl Starving Snickerfang 40 % , Snickerfang Hyena 40 % , Ravage 30 %\n2 Blasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %\nScorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %","desc":"It is a well known fact that hyenas possess tremendous strength in their jowls, but the strength to snap through three inches of thorium steel? Impossible, improbable, and yet I have seen this demonstrated with my own eyes.\nVenture forth, into the Blasted Lands, and bring me three snickerfang jowls. As you search for the snickerfang, be on the lookout for boars and scorpoks: The initial assay also requires two blasted boar lungs and one scorpok pincer to complete.","rew":"You will receive:\nR.O.I.D.S.\nExperience: 4,700","back":"You smell foul, ‹name›. Have you been traipsing in sulfur fields? And where are my components?!","done":"How do you feel, ‹name›? You radiate with the aura of the snickerfang--your strength, unmatched by mortals!\nUnfortunately, with the components you brought to me, I could only make enough of the assay for one tablet. I will require more components, should you require another tablet.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"96661":{"id":96661,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":45.4,"y":58,"n":"Pyall Silentstride","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97941":{"id":97941,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Jenna Lemkenilli in Auberdine in Darkshore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTeldrassil Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.2,"y":41,"n":"Jenna Lemkenilli","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96101":{"id":96101,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94261":{"id":94261,"t":"Craftsmans writ great rage potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Great Rage Potion\nGreat Rage Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Great Rage Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Great Rage Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94261","cats":["crafting"]},"94341":{"id":94341,"t":"Craftsmans writ sniper scope","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Sniper Scope\nSniper Scope","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Sniper Scope, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Sniper Scope Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94341","cats":["crafting"]},"7941":{"id":7941,"t":"More Armor Kits","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"8 Rugged Armor Kit Larion 10 % , Rabid Blisterpaw 0 % , Scorching Elemental 0 %","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","back":"‹name›, I must thank you for all your help. I have plenty of supplies, through no small efforts on your part, but if you wish to bring me more armor kits, then I will gladly trade them for Darkmoon Faire tickets.","done":"There you are, ‹name›. A fair trade. Enjoy.\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"6341":{"id":6341,"t":"The Bounty of Teldrassil","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Nessa's Collection to Vesprystus.\nNessa's Collection\nProvided: Nessa's Collection","desc":"The fishermen of Rut'theran village do very well, for the fish here are extremely large and abundant. I would like to compare the bounty here with that of the mainland.\nI have a collection of fish bones and scales that I would like taken to a colleague of mine in Darkshore. His name is Laird, he is a fish vendor in the village of Auberdine.\nBring my collection to our hippogryph master, Vesprystus, and speak to him about traveling to Auberdine.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"How may I help you? Are you in need of transport?","done":"Ah, you wish to get this to Auberdine? Very well...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.3,"y":92.4,"n":"Nessa Shadowsong","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.4,"y":94,"n":"Vesprystus","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1141":{"id":1141,"t":"The Family and the Fishing Pole","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Catch 6 Darkshore Grouper for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.\n6 Darkshore Grouper","desc":"I love fishing. The Blump family is known for fishing. My name is Gubber Blump; I fish.\nThere's a kind of fish I like to catch around these parts called Darkshore grouper. I used to go out on a boat to fish for grouper, but no boats have been going out since them mean ol' murlocs moved in. I bet they been eating up all the grouper too.\nSay, you wanna help me catch Darkshore grouper? I'd give you a bona fide Blump Family Fishing Pole if you did! It's a real good pole to catch fish with.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlump Family Fishing Pole\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"There's plenty of good dishes you use Darkshore groupers for. They're good to eat, but I think it's more fun catching them.\nYou caught any Darkshore groupers yet?","done":"Them's some real nice groupers, ‹name›! Thanks for helping me out!\nYou're at least as good of a fisherman as my cousin, Graun Blump. She also has a beard and she smells kinda funny, but that don't do nothing to stop her fishing. I reckon you have what it takes to use a Blump Family Fishing Pole.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.1,"y":44.9,"n":"Gubber Blump","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"741":{"id":741,"t":"The Absent Minded Prospector","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus.\nMysterious Fossil\nProvided: Mysterious Fossil","desc":"So the prospector wants to send the mysterious fossil to the Explorers' League in Darnassus? I don't feel right leaving Darkshore without him.\nHere, ‹name›, deliver the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHammerfist Gloves Windfelt Gloves Relic Hunter Belt\nExperience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"What can I do for you, ‹race›?","done":"Oh my! Leave it to Prospector Remtravel to discover such a find!\nDarkshore Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":41.8,"n":"Archaeologist Hollee","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":84.5,"n":"Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"981":{"id":981,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":31,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,500 experience instead of 2,540, 0.98 times as much.","obj":"Talk to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.","desc":"For all the work that you have done, you deserve to be well rewarded. Return to Delgren and tell him that Athrikus Narassin lies stilled by your hand, and the Cult of the Dark Strand is beaten and scattered.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPious Legwraps Seraph's Strike\nExperience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"I knew you would be up to the task, ‹name›.\nI sense great deeds before you, and that you will right many of the wrongs that plague our lands. Bear my blessings, ‹name›, as well as this gift.\nDarkshore Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98901":{"id":98901,"t":"Darkspear islands clash","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.\nIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Theramore Expeditionary Force\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98901","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"3781":{"id":3781,"t":"Morrowgrain Research","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Arch Druid's Seed Voucher to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus.\nSeed Voucher\nProvided: Seed Voucher","desc":"With what we call an Evergreen Pouch, we have cultivated Tharlendris seeds in the soil from Un'Goro Crater. These seeds blossom into an array of random, potent herbs. One result is morrowgrain, a mysterious herb we know little about; I intend to unravel this mystery.\nTake this to Mathrengyl downstairs, and he will give you some seeds so you can get started. If you run out, you will need to purchase more from him.","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Packet of Tharlendris Seeds\nExperience: 470\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Peace and serenity be yours, friend. You are here on business from the Arch Druid himself, yes?","done":"Yes, this voucher is good for twenty packets of seeds. If you run out, we have more that can be provided. Unfortunately though, Tharlendris seeds are quite costly to produce in significant numbers. This is why the Cenarion Circle asks that those who are assisting us help out by offsetting some of the cost.\nThose who return with morrowgrain find that the reward the Arch Druid offers far makes up for the cost.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"6661":{"id":6661,"t":"Deeprun Rat Roundup","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Capture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute. Lead the rats back to Monty. Don't forget to turn in the flute when you're finished.\nRat Catcher's Flute\nRats Captured : 0/ 5\nProvided: Rat Catcher's Flute","desc":"Avast ye scallywag. Arrrr... Arrrr ye looking fer work? We gots a serious rat problem down here an' not enough hands on the poop deck.\nWhat do ye say? All ye needs to do is take this here rat catchin' flute and play the melody around the vermin. They'll follow ye to the ends of the world!\nJust capture five of the little buggers and bring em back here. We needs em alive.\nArrrrr...","rew":"Experience: 900","back":"Yarrr... Swabby, what be takin' ye so long?","done":"These'll werk nicely, matey. Me brother needs em still tickin' and kickin,' else they go sour... Ye don't want to taste no sour rat kabob.\nAlterac Mountains Open the zone on the world map Start Monty , an item: Squirrel Token End Monty Level 12 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 15 18 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 6661\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 12, 990 XP in all.\n1 [ 12 ] Deeprun Rat Roundup this quest\nCapture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute.\nMonty\n900 XP\n2 [ 12 ] Me Brother, Nipsy\nTake the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot.\nMonty\n90 XP","cats":["deeprun-tram"]},"5381":{"id":5381,"t":"Hand of Iruxos","lv":38,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Demon Box from Thunder Axe Fortress, and return it, along with the Demon Pick to Taiga Wisemane in Shadowprey Village.\nDemon Box Demon Spirit\nDemon Pick\nProvided: Demon Pick","desc":"The Burning Blade possesses the Demon Box. Within it lies the powerful Hand of Iruxos. The Burning Blade uses it to open demonic portals at Mannoroc Coven. We must stop the tide of demons entering our world, ‹name›!\nUse this demon pick on the red crystal in Thunder Axe Fortress to gain access to the Demon Box.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, do you have the Demon Box?","done":"Ah, the Demon Box. Give it to me, ‹class›, and I shall open... and thus reveal to you the Hand of Iruxos.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":25.8,"y":68.2,"n":"Taiga Wisemane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"261":{"id":261,"t":"Down the Scarlet Path","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy 30 Undead Ravagers, then return to Brother Anton at Nijel's Point.\nUndead Ravager slain : 0/ 30","desc":"I will be frank. We are at war with the Scourge. It is an evil that corrupts our people and infects our land. It must be stopped before it overwhelms us and drags our world into shadow. We of the Scarlet Crusade have sworn to fight the Scourge with body and soul.\nIf you are with us, then gather your courage and prove your allegiance--destroy the undead ravagers of Desolace, in the Valley of Bones to the south.\nDo this, and the Crusade will embrace you.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000","back":"The Scourge grows in power with the passing of each day. If you truly wish to halt its advances, then show me.","done":"You have proven your resolve, and the Scarlet Crusade commends you.\nIf you do not shy from righteous slaughter, then perhaps your path lies with us...\nDesolace Shen'dralas","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.5,"y":7.9,"n":"Brother Anton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1381":{"id":1381,"t":"Khan Hratha","lv":42,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your Magram reputation, and bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\nMaraudine Key Fragment Khan Hratha\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"The Gelkis Khan is dead, and now the Maraudine will fall! Kill the Maraudine Khan, Hratha!\nTo face him, blow the horn on the high bluff in the Valley of Spears. But to blow the horn, you need a mouthpiece. To get a mouthpiece, kill Maraudine centaur. Keep killing until you find a mouthpiece. Then blow the horn.\nDo this and Maraudine centaur will come to the tower. Kill them until Khan Hratha appears. Hratha holds the piece of a key. Give this piece to me...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKolkar Hunter's Belt Ceremonial Centaur Blanket\nExperience: 4,300","back":"Do what I ask. Prove to me that you are an ally of the Magram!","done":"Khan Hratha is dead! Now the Magram are the strongest of the centaur! We will crush the others, and rule Desolace!\nWe will remember, you, ‹name›, and you will be spared our hooves when all others are trampled.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7461":{"id":7461,"t":"The Madness Within","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,250, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"You must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar. Once the Pylons have powered down, the force field surrounding Immol'thar will have dissipated.\nEnter the Prison of Immol'thar and eradicate the foul demon that stands at its heart. Finally, confront Prince Tortheldrin in Athenaeum.\nReturn to the Shen'dralar Ancient in the courtyard should you complete this quest.\nImmol'thar slain\nPrince Tortheldrin slain","desc":"Have you heard enough? Are you a man/woman of action?\nThis madness must come to an end. The age of the immortals has long since passed. Destroy the guardians surrounding the pylons to lower the force field. When this is done, destroy Immol'thar. With the Prince's power greatly reduced, attack and end him. Lay the spirits of this city to rest, adventurer.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"Be wary, adventurer. The Prince is... persuasive.","done":"We thank you, hero.\nSilverpine Forest Open the zone on the world map Start Shen'dralar Ancient End Shen'dralar Ancient Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 7461\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 60, 11,250 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Madness Within this quest\nYou must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Treasure of the Shen'dralar\nReturn to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n650 XP\n[ 60 ] The Treasure of the Shen'dralar\nReturn to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n650 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"5061":{"id":5061,"t":"Aquatic Form","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Idol of Shifting Tides.","obj":"Return to Darnassus and show Mathrengyl Bearwalker the Pendant of the Sea Lion.\nPendant of the Sea Lion\nProvided: Pendant of the Sea Lion","desc":"You have completed the necessary lessons all young druids are taught before they can adopt an aquatic aspect. Go now back to your trainer, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, in Darnassus. Show him your pendant and prove to him you are ready to learn what he has to teach you. He will complete your training, allowing you to become one with the water.\nGoodbye, young druid. We shall speak again.","rew":"New in Forever: Idol of Shifting Tides.\nYou will receive:\nAquarius Belt Idol of Shifting Tides\nYou will learn: Aquatic Form\nExperience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Your return to Darnassus is not without heralding, though I will need proof of your lessons learned in Moonglade before I will teach you your aquatic form.\nDo you have the Pendant of the Sea Lion?","done":"Very impressive, ‹name›. You are ready to learn your aquatic form, and it is my pleasure to teach it to you.\nAlso, in recognition of your achievement during the two trials, I give you this item. I hope you'll find it to be a welcome addition to your gear as a protector of nature and a keeper of the balance.\nMoonglade Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98341":{"id":98341,"t":"The great windborne cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek out the Avatar of Saeyleenan in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the windborne cat.","desc":"A spirit of your homeland has recently appeared here and has asked me to guide you to it. This windborne cat spirit has come to tutor and mentor you so that you may take the feline shape of the spirit on Zephras.\nAll druids eventually seek this wisdom, though it seems your homeland has a slightly different shape than our traditional one. If you desire to take this spirit's feline form, you will need to undergo our trial.\nIt can be found in the southern part of Moonglade, south of the twin bridges.","done":"Greetings, young shen'dorei. I have come to you because I sense you are ready to undertake the trial to determine if you understand my spiritual nature or not.\nI will have you take the trial of the Great Cat Spirit of Azeroth, but as you are from Zephras, I wished to oversee your progress myself. After all, it is my shape you would take, not that of a Azerothian cat spirit.\nLet us begin.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":44,"y":73.4,"n":"Avatar of Saeyleenan","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"5541":{"id":5541,"t":"Ammo for Rumbleshot","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Rumbleshot's Ammo to Hegnar Rumbleshot in Dun Morogh.\nRumbleshot's Ammo Ammo Crate","desc":"Hegnar Rumbleshot sells guns off the road to Anvilmar. Riflemen and mortar teams spend a lot of time practicing out near his shop, and he's always needing fresh ammunition.\nBut... the last crate of ammo I sent him got lost along the way. My courier said he was camped near the Grizzled Den when wendigo chased him away... and the fool left Rumbleshot's ammo behind!\n‹name›, can you get that ammo and take it to Rumbleshot? He's been waiting on it and I'm sure he's running low.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"I hope you're not here for ammo, because I'm almost out!","done":"Great, more ammo! Old Loslor's shipment finally came through! The ammo might be late, but just like my grand daddy used to tell me: late's better than never!\nThank you much, ‹name›. I already have buyers eager for this stuff!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":50.1,"y":49.4,"n":"Loslor Rudge","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":40.7,"y":65.1,"n":"Hegnar Rumbleshot","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96821":{"id":96821,"t":"Legging it","lv":6,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 6 Ridgeshade Creepers and 6 Ridgeshade Lurkers in southern Durotar, then report to Gar'thok in Razor Hill.\nRidgeshade Creeper slain : 0/ 6\nRidgeshade Lurker slain : 0/ 6","desc":"We be seein' fewer and fewer travelers from Razor Hill. The scorpids were never much fun, but now I be hearin' there be spiders makin' their nest along the road.\nIf your travels be takin' you up north, kill some of the spiders on your way. Then, let Razor Hill know the path's a bit safer for them.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"The peons have been scared to travel south for some time, Joruus. Now that you've cleared the path a bit, we can get them back to work.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.8,"y":74,"n":"Vel'rin Fang","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":43.4,"n":"Gar'Thok","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"101":{"id":101,"t":"The Totem of Infliction","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Ghoul Fangs, 10 Skeleton Fingers and 5 Vials of Spider Venom to Madame Eva in Darkshire.\n10 Ghoul Fang Fetid Corpse 80 % , Rotted One 80 % , Plague Spreader 80 % , Brain Eater 80 % and 2 more\n5 Vial of Spider Venom Carrion Recluse 80 % , Naraxis 80 % , Black Widow Hatchling 80 % , Green Recluse 80 % and 2 more\n10 Skeleton Finger Skeletal Raider 80 % , Skeletal Healer 80 % , Skeletal Warder 80 % , Skeletal Fiend 80 % and 3 more","desc":"As the mystical taint creeps through the forest, the need for self-protection is undeniable, ‹name›. The winds whisper to me and they speak of a great danger which waits patiently for you in the near future.\nIf you wish to protect yourself, noble ‹class›, bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom. For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.","rew":"You will receive:\nTotem of Infliction\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom. For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.","done":"Very wise of you, ‹name›. This Totem of Infliction will help to protect you against the evil which lurks throughout Azeroth and beyond. When you feel threatened, hold this totem and take comfort in its magical aura. Be brave, fair ‹class›. You will need all the courage you can muster for I see much bloodshed in your future.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"181":{"id":181,"t":"Look To The Stars","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Look To The Stars.","obj":"Locate Zzarc'Vul in the southern ogre mound in Duskwood and return his monocle to Viktori in Darkshire.\nOgre's Monocle Zzarc' Vul","desc":"Now there is just one more item needed to complete this device. Cog's blueprint calls for a lens of some sort. The only lens I know of that would be large enough will be very difficult to acquire.\nThere is an ogre by the name of Zzarc'Vul who resides in the mound in southern Duskwood. If you can, bring to me his monocle and I will use that as our lens!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZodiac Gloves Belt of the Stars\nExperience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Were you able to convince Zzarc'Vul to lend us his monocle for our experiment?","done":"At last! The stargazing device is complete! Thank you, ‹name›. Now I can continue my research. . .","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":79.8,"y":48,"n":"Viktori Prism'Antras","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"7541":{"id":7541,"t":"Service to the Horde","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 40 instead of 45.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Allegiance Lonetree's Circle\nMoney: 1 50 1 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"It will take time for our scholars to study the pendant you brought us. But for your service to the Horde I would like to offer you a small token.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your acts bring honor to you, and to us.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Zor Lonetree","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6021":{"id":6021,"t":"Zaeldarr the Outcast","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Zaeldarr's Head to Caretaker Alen at Light's Hope Chapel.\nZaeldarr's Head Zaeldarr the Outcast","desc":"Can you believe that, after all the trouble we have in the plaguelands... we have to worry about thieves too? And not just normal thieves, troll thieves.\nAnd not just normal troll thieves. Dead troll thieves!\nThey're led by this big, dead troll named Zaeldarr the Outcast, and they come here at night and steal bodies from the pit below, then take them back to their evil, dead troll hideout--the Undercroft to the west.\nGo there and take out Zaeldarr, ‹name›. I'm sick to death of his mischief!","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200\n+75 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Did you find the hideout, ‹name›? Did you take care of Zaeldarr?","done":"Great, you got him! And I hope you taught his gang a lesson too!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":69.9,"y":53.7,"n":"Caretaker Alen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5781":{"id":5781,"t":"Of Forgotten Memories","lv":57,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Undercroft - at the southernmost section of the Eastern Plaguelands - and recover Taelan's Hammer. Return to Tirion Fordring upon completion of your objective.\nTaelan's Hammer Mercutio Filthgorger","desc":"To help Taelan regain what he has lost, you must gather items from his past.\nThe first such item is a toy that I gave to him on his 7th birthday. It was his most cherished possession: A miniature war hammer; an exact replica of my very own.\nAfter I was banished for treason, his mother told him that I had died. He was taken to my false grave at the Undercroft, where he buried the hammer along with my memory - forever.\nYou must venture to the Undercroft and recover Taelan's hammer.","rew":"Experience: 6,000","back":"He must be redeemed.","done":"<Tirion blinks to hold back tears.>\nIt was destiny that we meet, ‹name›. You have blessed me with your kindness.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5941":{"id":5941,"t":"Return to Chromie","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Bundle of Relics to Chromie in Andorhal.\nBundle of Relics\nProvided: Bundle of Relics","desc":"You have gathered many relics of the battle of Darrowshire. Each time you returned with more, my heart yearned for my village... yearned to protect it from its fate.\nI know that cannot be, but Chromie, that strange gnome in Andorhal, tells me it is possible. She says you can save Darrowshire!\nShe asked me to gather together the relics, and to have you bring them to her. She said that she awaits you in the ruined inn of Andorhal.","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"I have been in contact with your friend Carlin. He feels great pain for the doom of his village, but he speaks very highly of you and knows that you can set things right.\nOh, but I'm drifting from the subject at hand... ‹name›, do you have the relics I asked for?","done":"Ah yes, there they are. Together they weave a powerful spell, one that will raise the spirits of Darrowshire.\nWith that spell, and with a little luck, we can save Joseph Redpath!\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9221":{"id":9221,"t":"Superior Armaments of Battle - Friend of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 30 Insignias of the Dawn and 30 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n30 Insignia of the Dawn\n30 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of power?\nI must warn you; purchases made at a friendly reputation with the Dawn come with a hefty surcharge. I would advise that you gain a better reputation with the Dawn before moving forward with your plans.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Piety Band of Resolution Verimonde's Last Resort Supply Bag Leggings of the Plague Hunter Sanctified Leather Helm\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9141":{"id":9141,"t":"They Call Me \"The Rooster\"","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dispatch Commander Metz at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants an Argent Dawn Valor Token.\nArgent Dawn Valor Token","desc":"You want a writ? What? Do you expect me to hand you a highly sought after work order just for showing up? I think not, scrub. Crafters from around the world bid for jobs here at the front lines.\nIf you want a work order, you'll have to show me that you're willing to bleed for the cause. Bring me a valor token and we'll talk.\nAnd there's only one way to get your grubby little scrub mitts on those - get to killin'.","rew":"You will receive:\nSealed Craftsman's Writ\nExperience: 3,300\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Commander Metz chews on his cigar.>\nWhat is it? I'm a busy man.","done":"Alright, here's how it works: For every valor token that you turn in, I'll give you another writ. You complete the order on that writ and deliver the order to Packmaster Stonebruiser. Got it? Good. Now get out of here.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":48,"n":"Dispatch Commander Metz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"21":{"id":21,"t":"Skirmish at Echo Ridge","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Kobold Laborers, then return to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey.\nKobold Laborer slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Your previous investigations are proof that the Echo Ridge Mine needs purging. Return to the mine and help clear it of kobolds.\nWaste no time, ‹name›. The longer the kobolds are left unmolested in the mine, the deeper a foothold they gain in Northshire.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOutfitter Belt Outfitter Boots Outfitter Gloves\nExperience: 450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I know it's bloody work, ‹name›, but it's vital to the safety of Northshire. Are you ready to report?","done":"Once again, you have earned my respect, and the gratitude of the Stormwind Army. There may yet be kobolds in the mine, but I will marshal others against them. We have further tasks for you.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4181":{"id":4181,"t":"Goblin Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Goblin Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Expert engineering yields two distinct disciplines: gnome and goblin. I only bother to mention goblin engineering because I'm a fair trainer. They like to make things that blow up, and they rarely care what is in the way - even themselves.\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn how to blow yourself up, then take it to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure this is what you want before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"I can smell fresh recruits much like I can an excellent blasting powder - from a mile away. Have you come seeking to learn about the mastery of the explosion?","done":"Well ‹name›, you were wise to seek my tutelage! Any schlep can become an expert at the basics of engineering - the gnomes and their irradiated home of Gnomeregan are proof of that. It takes a strong mind and a steady hand (emphasis on STEADY) though to master the discipline of Goblin Engineering.\nKeep your ears perked ‹name›, and you might learn something.\nStormwind City Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.1,"y":30.3,"n":"Lilliam Sparkspindle","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4421":{"id":4421,"t":"The Corruption of the Jadefire","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 11 Jadefire Felsworns, 9 Jadefire Shadowstalkers, 9 Jadefire Rogues, and Xavathras. Return to Eridan Bluewind in Felwood when the task has been completed.\nJadefire Felsworn slain : 0/ 11\nJadefire Shadowstalker slain : 0/ 9\nJadefire Rogue slain : 0/ 9\nXavathras slain","desc":"Not many seek adventure here... Felwood's corruption is widespread and indiscriminate.\nAs part of the Emerald Circle, I seek to heal this land, but there are some that wish it to fester.\nThe ones I speak of are the Jadefire satyrs that dwell to the northwest of here, at the Ruins of Constellas. Led by a particularly cruel satyr named Xavathras, they continue to spread the disease to any creatures they encounter.\nWe must defend this land that was once ours. Defeat Xavathras and destroy his minions.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"The corruption here drives the creatures into madness...","done":"Ridding Felwood of Xavathras is only the first step in a long process. It will take much work to repair the damage that has been done here.\nI sense that there is something much larger than just the satyrs at work here, but we will only know the truth with time...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4101":{"id":4101,"t":"Cleansing Felwood","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Blood Amber to Arathandris Silversky in Felwood.\n15 Blood Amber Dessecus 80 % , Warpwood Shredder 80 % , Warpwood Moss Flayer 80 %","desc":"Plants give life to Felwood, yet even they suffer the taint of corruption. I know ways to cleanse them, but I cannot give out such knowledge to those I don't know or trust. Prove to me that you will truly aid the cause of the Cenarion Circle!\nTo the north lie the Irontree Caverns. The Warpwood elementals present there are now beyond hope of cleansing. I ask you to bring me their sap - blood amber it is called - so I may study it in the hopes of saving other forms of life here.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"I know Felwood suffers, ‹name› - I suffer along with it! I must remain steadfast in my conviction; were the knowledge I possess to fall into the wrong hands, it would spell disaster for all of Felwood.\nBring to me the blood amber drawn from the slain Warpwood elementals, and I will trust you enough to help me enact a means to fight the corruption.","done":"This blood amber will be used to find a means of defeating the corruption present in Felwood. You've proven to me that you're willing to do whatever it takes for the Cenarion Circle. I trust you now, friend.\nIt might seem odd that killing the elementals proved yourself to me, but the end of saving countless sentient beings must justify the means we take. You and I can now focus on the preservation of life through the salves I can make.\n‹name›, the time has come to cleanse Felwood.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4261":{"id":4261,"t":"Ancient Spirit","lv":56,"min":49,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Arei to safety, then speak with Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song, in eastern Ashenvale.","desc":"Felwood was once a peaceful and serene land... Until the legion took hold. The infernals, destruction, chaos...\nThe skull of Gul'dan ensured that none were spared here. All fell to the corruption.\nEven now, as a spirit, I still find myself trapped, bearing the suffering of this land. Help me find my way home. Please, ‹name›, tell me you will lead an ancient spirit away from here, where I may finally rest.\nOnce I am free, seek out Kayneth Stillwind, a druid that resides in Forest Song, to the east.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEthereal Mist Cape Clouddrift Mantle\nExperience: 7,300\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Yes, ‹name›. Felwood has been through much hardship. Thank you for what you have done.\nOne day, we may be able to reclaim Felwood from the corruption; every kind deed helps.\nAshenvale Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":85.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Kayneth Stillwind","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4741":{"id":4741,"t":"Wild Guardians","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Trull Failbane in Felwood wants you to hunt 13 Moontouched Owlbeasts.\nMoontouched Owlbeast slain : 0/ 13","desc":"In the northern areas of Winterspring, the Wildkin grow even more ferocious. We must continue our measures there.\nHunt the moontouched owlbeasts in Winterspring, and explore the area they inhabit.\nThis is dangerous ground, but I know that you will be able to handle the challenge. Return to me after you have slain 13 of the wildkin.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Don't tell me that you're too scared! Get going!","done":"I sense that you are enjoying your work. And I believe that we are onto something here.\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.7,"y":52.8,"n":"Trull Failbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2821":{"id":2821,"t":"The Mark of Quality","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Yeti Hides to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n10 Thick Yeti Hide Bloodroar the Stalker 60 % , Lurking Feral Scar 60 % , Enraged Feral Scar 60 % , Hulking Feral Scar 60 % and 1 more","desc":"My philosophy on leatherworking is that the work must be the best quality possible - no compromises. Anyone who says that quality doesn't matter is trying to sell you ocean-front property in Dun Morogh!\nIn my latest pursuit of high-quality materials, I have run across thick yeti hides. The Yeti are native to Feralas, with many found in Feral Scar Vale. I want some, and I'll give you a choice of one of my leather goods for a stack of ten. If that sounds fair to you, then we're in business.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPratt's Handcrafted Boots Pratt's Handcrafted Gloves\nExperience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"A stack of ten thick yeti hides will net you a choice of one of my crafted items. Because I care about quality, I am able to ensure you'll get a good item!\nIf you can't seem to find yetis, I know where some might be. Try looking just inland of the Forgotten Coast, around Feral Scar Vale.","done":"Did you stop and examine the texture of these hides? Properly treated, these hides could very well be stronger than iron. Not many people know about these hides, and that in combination with the vast treating solutions I know will allow me to potentially make items with a true mark of quality... thanks to you, of course!\nAnd now, please choose from what I am able to offer you for your service!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"501":{"id":501,"t":"Elixir of Pain","lv":24,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Trophy Belt. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring 10 vials of Mountain Lion Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\n10 Mountain Lion Blood Starving Mountain Lion 15 % , Feral Mountain Lion 15 % , Mountain Lion 15 % , Hulking Mountain Lion 15 %","desc":"Oh, ‹name›. . .the flowers are blooming in Hillsbrad and the air is so fresh and brisk. I can't help but to wallow in the misery of it all. I look out my grimy window and long for the day when our New Plague brings this world the death it deserves.\nAs much as I would love to sit and brood all day, my duty to the Dark Lady calls. Help me, would you? My research leads me to believe I can make the most splendid death-brew with the blood of a Mountain Lion. Bring some to me and we'll have a little fun.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGloves of Brawn Stomping Boots Firewalker Boots Trophy Belt\nNew in Forever: Trophy Belt.\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Hot Lion Chops\nExperience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I remember you, ‹name›. You were going to help me out in concocting my latest elixir. I'll need that blood before I can bring my own special brand of misery to the inhabitants of Hillsbrad.","done":"Superb collecting, ‹name›.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"661":{"id":661,"t":"Hints of a New Plague?","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,550 experience instead of 3,350, 1.06 times as much.","obj":"Find Phin Odelic in Southshore.","desc":"I've seen Kinelory look way worse after a night in the tavern than she does now. You obviously did a good job protecting her.\nThese items she brought back from the farm should at least let Phin get an idea of what's going on out here in Arathi. Just to make sure there's no retaliation after your attack, we're going to stay here for a bit longer. Would you be willing to head back to Southshore and talk to Phin?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDustfall Robes Lightstep Leggings\nExperience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","done":"So, the two troublemakers are all right after all? Haha, I'm glad to hear it. I thank you for bringing me news of their whereabouts and status--it pleases me greatly that they are still alive; the two of them are irreplaceable as friends and traveling companions.\nBut... it's more important I thank you properly for your help. Here. Take this along with my group's thanks.\nWith any luck, we'll figure out what the Forsaken are up to, and put an end to it.\nArathi Highlands Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.8,"n":"Quae","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.3,"y":59,"n":"Phin Odelic","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6101":{"id":6101,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Nightsaber Stalker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"The variance of nature is something that can be relied upon, ‹name›. It is predictable in the way that it never remains the same; it is always changing.\nThe tasks I give to you will help you to see and appreciate the vast differences of the creatures you may choose as your companion.\nTake this taming rod and use it to tame a nightsaber stalker, found to the south. Practice your skills as a hunter. Then you will begin to understand the similarities and differences of nature.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Understanding the balance between nature and oneself is a way of life for every ‹race›.","done":"I see your commitment and that you have understood what I have taught you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9301":{"id":9301,"t":"Envelope from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Bloodstained Envelope to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Bloodstained Envelope\nProvided: A Bloodstained Envelope","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"3461":{"id":3461,"t":"Return to Tymor","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Tymor's Drawing Kit to him in Ironforge.\nDrawing Kit\nProvided: Drawing Kit","desc":"Tymor didn't give me anything to pay you with, so I suggest you take it up with him when you get back to Ironforge. I'm sure he'll still be in his place in the Mystic Ward. Just go knockin' and make sure he pays you good. This place ain't no picnic... that's for sure.\nThanks again for helping him out though, and good luck.\nOh, and I don't need the drawing kit. Why don't you just bring it back to Tymor when you go to see him?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSteelsmith Greaves Skullspell Orb\nExperience: 7,600\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You're back! Excellent. Do you have my drawing kit also?","done":"Wonderful! I'm so glad to hear it.\nI'm really excited to get to my tower and go over those rubbings. I'm so envious of you... going to a place like Azshara. That's any student of the arcane's dream, I would guess.\nWell, we never spoke about any kind of reward since you were just working for the Explorer's League, but you deserve something.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.1,"y":21.9,"n":"Tymor","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"3701":{"id":3701,"t":"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes and recover information from the Thaurissan Relics. Return to Royal Historian Archesonus when you have recovered the information.\nInformation Recovered : 0/ 12","desc":"Venture to the smoldering ruins of Thaurissan in the Burning Steppes and gather as much information as possible.\nIt is said that mysterious relics litter the ruins. Perhaps you should start your search there, ‹name›. Beware the Thaurissan guardians: Assassins that guard the ruins, keeping whatever secrets may still be buried there protected.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of the Aristocrat\nMoney: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you bring new information?","done":"Oh my! This information explains quite a lot about Thaurissan.\nThere is much more to learn!\nDun Morogh Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.2,"y":30,"n":"Royal Historian Archesonus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"5141":{"id":5141,"t":"Dragonscale Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Tough Scorpid Breastplates, 2 Tough Scorpid Gloves, and 10 Worn Dragonscales to Peter Galen in Azshara.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Dragonscale Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Elemental Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\n2 Tough Scorpid Breastplate\n2 Tough Scorpid Gloves\n10 Worn Dragonscale Jademir Oracle 2.4 % , Dreamstalker 2.2 % , Verdantine Oracle 2 % , Verdantine Boughguard 1.9 %","desc":"Dragonscale leatherworking isn't easy, but it's extremely rewarding. I'll teach you how to make this fine mail armor, but only if you agree to certain conditions.\nBy choosing this path, you agree never to learn elemental or tribal leatherworking; there is only room for one of the three at the apex of the craft. Furthermore, I'll need some samples of your best work involving scorpid armor. Finally, I'll need proof of your ability to acquire the staple of the trade: scales of the dragonkin.","rew":"You will learn: Dragonscale Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Dragonscale","back":"If you're ready to commit to a permanent decision by becoming a dragonscale leatherworker, then I'm ready to take you on as a student. Just bring to me the things I asked for, and we'll begin your education.","done":"I'll hand it to you - it takes a strong will to make a permanent decision like you've just done. I assure you, dragonscale leatherworking will prove to be a profitable and rewarding path for you to follow.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":37.6,"y":65.4,"n":"Peter Galen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"2501":{"id":2501,"t":"Badlands Reagent Run II","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the empty thaumaturgy vessels on scorched guardian dragons found in the Badlands. Once you have them filled, bring them to Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar.\n3 Vessel of Dragon's Blood\nProvided: Thaumaturgy Vessel Lockbox","desc":"You have been most helpful to me, ‹name›. I would like to reward you with the very recipe for the brew I gave you earlier, but I must ask of you a favor that is quite dangerous.\nThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon. Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be careful. Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.\nDo this, and the recipe will be yours.","rew":"Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need? Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success. Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...","done":"From one alchemist to another, I salute you. Here, take this recipe and commit it to your knowledge. May it bring you the success and rewards that it has brought me over the years!\nLoch Modan Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.1,"y":49.4,"n":"Ghak Healtouch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1861":{"id":1861,"t":"Mirror Lake","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Mirror Lake sample to Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.\nMirror Lake Water Sample\nProvided: Jennea's Flask","desc":"This world has been victim to massive mystic struggles, which tore magic currents from once stable channels. We struggle to determine the effects these changes have caused, and some of us fear the worst!\nBut I will reveal more of this later. Right now, we need you to gather information.\nHere, take this flask. Go to the base of the waterfall at Mirror Lake, southwest of the Stormwind gates, and retrieve a sample of the water there. Return it to me so that I might test it for magical taints.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLey Orb Ley Staff\nExperience: 850","back":"Do you have the sample, ‹name›? The flow of magic in Stormwind and Elwynn has been altered, and I must know if it is seeping into the water.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I will test this water for magical properties. Let us hope that it contains none, or we may find that those who drink from Mirror Lake for too long will be adversely affected.\nHere, ‹name›. Take this orb or staff as a token of your service. May it serve you well.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1941":{"id":1941,"t":"Manaweave Robe","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nManaweave Robe\nExperience: 1,050","done":"Here is your robe. It's one of my best made yet! Wear it with pride, and when people ask... tell them you got it at the Larson Clothiers!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":83.5,"n":"Wynne Larson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"8741":{"id":8741,"t":"The Champion Returns","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Green Scepter Shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris.\nGreen Scepter Shard\nProvided: Green Scepter Shard","desc":"The keeper awaits your return, ‹name›. Take the green scepter shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"Your deeds will be known to all, champion. They will sing your praises from Orgrimmar to the far reaches of the South Seas. All will know of the champion of the Bronze Flight, ‹name›.\nMoonglade Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"96261":{"id":96261,"t":"The broodmother","lv":31,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill Broodmother Valraxx at Gloomrise.\nBroodmother Valraxx slain","desc":"As is often the case with infestations such as the one we are facing at Gloomrise, a single powerful matriarch often leads to the rapid spread of a hostile spider population.\nIf we wish to drive these beasts off for good, we'll need to seek out the progenitor and end her. When you go to Gloomrise, seek out the broodmother there and destroy her. I'd advise you to bring allies, and be ready for anything. These seem to be no ordinary spiders.","rew":"You will receive:\nTransformative Cocoon\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Muln Earthfury","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9061":{"id":9061,"t":"Cryptstalker Wristguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Cryptstalker Wristguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Wristguards, 6 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Wristguards Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Wristguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Wristguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"2981":{"id":2981,"t":"A Threat in Feralas","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Belgrom Rockmaul wants you to speak with Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache.","desc":"Feralas is an ideal location for an accomplished ‹class› to prove himself/herself. A tribe of ogres called the Gordunni are the dominant military force there, and their numbers are growing. They must be stopped before they threaten our presence in Feralas.\nA warrior I know of named Rok Orhan resides at Camp Mojache in Feralas; go to her. She will tell you more of the situation when you arrive.","rew":"Experience: 900\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"So, Belgrom sent you. You are just in time, ‹race›.\nLet me explain the situation, and then you can decide if you are up to the challenge... But if Belgrom sent you, I am sure your courage is unquestionable.\nOrgrimmar Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1781":{"id":1781,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Symbol of Life to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.\nProvided: Symbol of Life","desc":"Take this, ‹name›. It is called the Symbol of Life.\nYou've proven charitable and patient, and now the time has come to see if you're powerful enough to focus one of the Light's greatest gifts.\nMy friend Gazin returned recently from an encounter with some Defias in Elwynn near Heroes' Vigil--he barely escaped with his life. He's near the altar having his wounds healed by our priests.\nTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May you bask in the Light's glory.","done":"*cough*\nPleasure to meet you, ‹race›. Don't mind my wounds, the good priest here can take care of ol' Gazin this time. I won't be needing the power of that Symbol of Life you've got there... not yet anyway.\nSo, Duthorian sent you to speak to me, huh? Fair enough. I'll tell you exactly what befell me and my friend Henze. And with any luck, and some skill on your part, perhaps you can still help us all.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45,"n":"Gazin Tenorm","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"91861":{"id":91861,"t":"Into fenris keep","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Investigate Fenris Keep to the north and attempt to locate the missing member of the Earthen Ring party.","desc":"<The fact that you only found only one body is a hopeful sign. Perhaps the High Elf that Trevan and Hadrec described is still alive somewhere deeper inside the nearby fortress?>","done":"You are one of the Forsaken, yes? Can you help free me?\nTime is short for me, I am afraid. Please hurry!","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65,"y":34.2,"n":"Charred Remains","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65.6,"y":23.2,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5621":{"id":5621,"t":"Garments of the Moon","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Sentinel Shaya and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar.\nHeal and fortify Sentinel Shaya","desc":"I need your help, ‹name›. I am needed here to train the other students, but you, you can help one of our injured Sentinels just south of Dolanaar. She was hurt patrolling the town and could use our aid. Her name is Shaya.\nWhen you find her, heal her wounds, and then fortify her body with your spells. This will at least protect her from harm longer if she finds trouble. Return to me here after you've done your duty to Elune.","rew":"You will receive:\nMoon Robes of Elune\nExperience: 270","back":"Our spells of Fortify are very powerful, Delor. They allow our companions to take further injury from all types of attacks and survive in situations where they would normally fall. But this is nothing when compared to our abilities to heal. There are no greater healers than a priest--do well to remember that. Your power alone can turn the tides of battle easily.","done":"You have done well and you have served Elune. For that, I thank you.\nPlease, take this robe as a token of my thanks. It signifies you have earned your place among our order. If you wish, wear it with pride, but either way, we will always recognize you as one of our own.\nGo with Elune, ‹name›, and thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.7,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94821":{"id":94821,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young ‹race›. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priestess Mims--she will tell you more.\nThe Light be with you, ‹name›.\nStormwind City Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"7621":{"id":7621,"t":"A Warning","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"‹class›, you are about to undergo a rigorous series of events which shall test all of your abilities.\nI suggest that you listen to the story that I have to tell.\nBe warned, you must complete this task alone. It is recommended that your allies remain at a distance. Interference by outside agents will result in a most severe punishment.\nDestiny has led you and you alone here. Battle with honor. Harness the Light.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":17.2,"y":12.8,"n":"Eris Havenfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1221":{"id":1221,"t":"Blueleaf Tubers","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,000 experience instead of 2,100, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Grab a Crate with Holes.\nGrab a Snufflenose Command Stick.\nGrab and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual.\nIn Razorfen Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher, and use the Command Stick on the gopher to make it search for Tubers.\nBring 6 Blueleaf Tubers, the Snufflenose Command Stick and the Crate with Holes to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\n6 Blueleaf Tuber Blueleaf Tuber in Razorfen Kraul\nCrate With Holes Crate with Holes\nSnufflenose Owner's Manual Snufflenose Owner's Manual\nSnufflenose Command Stick Snufflenose Command Sticks","desc":"Blueleaf tubers are a delicacy around the world! But they're rare, very rare. The only place to find them is here in the Barrens, deep in the earth, in Razorfen Kraul.\nAnd even then, they're impossible to find unless you know just where to look! That's why I've trained these snufflenose gophers to find them for me. They have great noses and can smell a tuber from fifty paces away.\nIt won't be easy, but if you get me some tubers I'll pay you handsomely.","rew":"You will receive:\nA Small Container of Gems\nExperience: 5,000\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Do you have the tubers, ‹name›?","done":"Great, you got them! I can sell these to my contacts for a bundle!\nThanks for the delivery, ‹name›! You are a great partner.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"8821":{"id":8821,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Darnassus. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.9,"y":33.4,"n":"Ironforge Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Lunalight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"78261":{"id":78261,"t":"The horn of xelthos","lv":23,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find The Horn of Xelthos inside of Shadowfang Keep. Then, return it to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village. You must complete the job alone.\nHorn of Xelthos\nFind Veenix","desc":"<A note sits in the chest>\nHello, ‹name›.\nI desire a treasure known as The Horn of Xelthos, which is somewhere within Shadowfang Keep.\nVenturing inside the keep usually calls for backup. However, for this job, a low profile is of utmost importance.\nYou must go alone.\nI have a contact, by the name of Veenix, in the Stonetalon Mountains. He should be able to help you get past the courtyard gate. The rest is up to you.\nReturn the horn here, and your payment will be sent soon after.\n- C","back":"<The chest sits, empty.>","done":"<You place The Horn of Xelthos into the chest>\nSilverpine Forest Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":47.1,"y":71.1,"n":"Dead Drop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"92421":{"id":92421,"t":"Light's Justice","lv":22,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Collect 25 Intact Limbs within The Ruins of Lordaeron for Morbin Lightbane in the Undercity.\n25 Intact Limbs","desc":"As a paladin of the Forsaken, it is my duty to exact the will of our Dark Lady while tending to our people's needs. We are fortunate with an opportunity to accomplish both.\nAbove the Undercity, the scourge still roam unchecked in great numbers. Our forces dwindle trying to reclaim our land, and decaying flesh cannot be reknit. Not without replacements.\nWould that our glorious captain Garek Bandarion still be with us, I know what he would wish. To finish what he started and heal our kin. For Lordaeron!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThe Stitcher Spare Part Bindings\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,600\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"What remains of the invading scourge? Have you managed to find suitable replacement parts?","done":"Let those who fall from the Banshee Queen's grace meet our justice!\nWith these parts, our brothers and sisters have hope to see another day. You do Captain Bandarion proud.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":89.8,"n":"Morbin Lightbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"7701":{"id":7701,"t":"WANTED: Overseer Maltorius","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deep within the Slag Pit of the Cauldron, in the Searing Gorge, you will find the traitorous Dark Iron dwarf named Overseer Maltorius.\nSlay Overseer Maltorius and take his head. Return the head to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker in the Searing Gorge for your reward.\nHead of Overseer Maltorius Overseer Maltorius","desc":"By order o' 'is eminence, Overseer Oilfist, the rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent an' newly hired commander o' the Dark Iron Slag Pit crew o' the Cauldron, Overseer Maltorius, is to be killed an' 'is head brung back as proof o' the deed.\nSee Lookout Captan Lolo Longstriker fer the reward on this bounty.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSeared Mail Vest Charred Leather Tunic\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Can't ya shee I'm bushy? What *hic* ish it ya be wantin? *hic*","done":"I never thunk I'd be lookin' at thish ugly mug again!\nHe acshually looksh better without the resht o' him attached.\nHere's yer reward *hic*, ‹race›.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":37.6,"y":26.5,"n":"Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":37.7,"y":26.6,"n":"Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8901":{"id":8901,"t":"Dearest Elenia,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Carefully Written Letter to Elenia Haydon near the bank in the Undercity.\nCarefully Written Letter\nProvided: Carefully Written Letter","desc":"Have you ever known love, young one? It was a thing foreign to me until lately, when I met a girl from the Undercity, Elenia. It is rare enough for one of my kind to look outside our own, let alone one of the Forsaken.\nBut now thoughts of her occupy my mind both days and nights.\nIf you can, could you take this letter to her? I want her to come here to Mulgore. I hope that she will say yes.","back":"Oh, and to what do I owe this pleasure?","done":"What kind words Temma writes for me. But, as much as his words move me, I cannot consider the love of a tauren. In thoughts, body and mind we are too different.\nIt is good I do not have to receive these thoughts of his in person. I could not bear to break his heart.\nThunder Bluff Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.8,"y":60.1,"n":"Temma of the Wells","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":66.9,"y":45.2,"n":"Elenia Haydon","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8981":{"id":8981,"t":"Gift Giving","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Gift Collection","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Handful of Rose Petals 5 Silver Shafted Arrow\nYou will also receive:\nBox of Chocolates","back":"Have you come to deliver a present of love and adoration to your favorite leader?","done":"Wonderful! Wonderful! I will add this to the pile of other gifts.\nI didn't expect so many! You must truly love your leaders.\nNow, let me just add one more to the count...\nUndercity Darnassus Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":55.2,"y":89.9,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.1,"y":80.5,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.5,"y":30.2,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7061":{"id":7061,"t":"The Feast of Winter Veil","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Feel free to read the book, \"The Feast of Winter Veil\", to learn more about the holiday. When you are finished with the book, deliver it to Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.\nThe Feast of Winter Veil\nProvided: The Feast of Winter Veil","desc":"Here - if you are interested in learning more about the Feast of Winter Veil, read this book. While I think our recognition of the legend is the appropriate one, I'm enough of a student of legends to appreciate the collection of all information into a single source.\nWhen you're done, take the book to Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff. I know for a fact he'd be interested in hearing that others have taken an interest in the lore of our people.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I bid you welcome to Mulgore and our humble community of Thunder Bluff, friend. I always take an interest in those who choose to take an interest in the kingdom, its people, and its lore. Is this why you are standing before me?","done":"The legends and lore surrounding the Winter Veil are ones that have faded from the forefront of public thought over the years. Yes, I know that the goblins are helping to revive the season for their own ends, the fact that our people reflect upon it at least in some form does good to keep such lore alive.\nYour desire to go beyond the material and learn about our past is an admirable trait, young ‹class›. I salute your wisdom.\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.7,"y":35.9,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":60.3,"y":51.7,"n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"98581":{"id":98581,"t":"Archaic rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Archaic Rune and speak to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.\nProvided: Archaic Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. Based on the Wildhammer style to these inscriptions, I'm guessin' this came from the shaman trainer Teo Hammerstorm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","back":"Ah, you were able to read the rune? It is imbued with the power of elements from some of our oldest script. That shows that you have the makings of a ‹class›.","done":"The shamanic arts have been kept by the Wildhammer clan for years, an' now those arts have passed into the care of the Bronzebeard dwarves as well. I'm here ta help spread these teachings an' offer guidance for new shamans learning the ways of the elements. Come ta me if ya need more trainin' in the spells of earth, air, fire, an' water.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.8,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94501":{"id":94501,"t":"Call of water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.\nProvided: Vial of Purest Water","desc":"Norric will have one more task for ye before rewarding ye with the water totem rites. The vial of water I've given ye is necessary for whatever that task is. Go now and find him. We shall meet again some day.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Sapta\nExperience: 460","back":"Hello again, Theinn. Yer looking well.\nWhat brings you back to me so soon?","done":"Ahh, water blessed by Hervdana herself, and gathered by your own hands? A gift indeed.\nThese vials shall birth your sapta, letting you glimpse the water spirits at Stendel's Pond, near Moonbrook. The last few drops of the water have an equally important purpose... waste not even a cork stopper dampened with sacred water.\nWetlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":65.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Hervdana Saegrund","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8341":{"id":8341,"t":"Lords of the Council","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Large Brilliant Shards and 3 Abyssal Signets to Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\n5 Large Brilliant Shard\n3 Abyssal Signet The Duke of Cynders , The Duke of Fathoms , The Duke of Shards , The Duke of Zephyrs","desc":"Lords of the Abyssal Council can only be summoned through the greater wind stones, and only the top ranking members of the Twilight's Council may speak to them. But... I have found a way to upgrade your disguise and fool the Abyssal Lords!\nThe disguise calls for a ring of lordship, worn only by the highest members of the cult. I will craft one for you if you can bring me large brilliant shards and abyssal signets.","rew":"You will receive:\nTwilight Cultist Ring of Lordship\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Do you have the shards and the signets, ‹name›? I will need them to create the ring of lordship.","done":"Thanks. Just one moment and I'll have that ring ready for you...\nThere it is. Now you're ready.\nBe sure to wear this ring, along with a medallion of station and the rest of the twilight trappings, when you activate a greater wind stone. Do that, and the Abyssal Council will think you one of their servants. Then, perhaps you can lure one into an ambush!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8501":{"id":8501,"t":"Target: Hive'Ashi Stingers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 30 Hive'Ashi Stingers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing XII in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing XII\nHive'Ashi Stinger slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing XII","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of the airborne Hive'Ashi stingers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You wish to tell me something, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Ashi has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"421":{"id":421,"t":"Prove Your Worth","lv":10,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 12 instead of 9. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher wants you to kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.\nMoonrage Whitescalp slain : 0/ 5","desc":"Lady Sylvanas has charged Varimathras with the conquering of the human and dwarven lands to the south.\nBut that fool, Arugal -- charlatan of Dalaran and now cursed beast of Shadowfang Keep -- let his reckless magic wreak havoc with the strategic stronghold of Silverpine Forest.\nI need someone skilled in the ways of combat to help clean up Arugal's mess. Prove yourself to me by killing 5 Moonrage Whitescalps. The wretched beasts can often be found just off the road, down the hill below.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"If you wish to prove yourself to me, you must kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps. Accomplish that task, and I will see to it your skill is put to more worthy assignments.","done":"You have served me well, ‹class›. It is obvious to me that you will be a worthy aide to me as I prepare to rid Silverpine Forest of Arugal's curse.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"3221":{"id":3221,"t":"Speak with Renferrel","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.","desc":"While you were out helping our deathstalkers, Apothecary Renferrel sent you a summons. He did not give me details, but he wanted to speak with you about the wolf hearts you had given him.","rew":"Experience: 90\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ah, very good. There is a matter regarding the wolf hearts you brought to me earlier that demands our attention.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"3861":{"id":3861,"t":"CLUCK!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find some Special Chicken Feed and return to your befriended chicken. When you find it, /cheer at it before trying to give it the Special Chicken Feed.\nSpecial Chicken Feed sold by Farmer Saldean","desc":"\"Cluck... cluck... cluck... BACAW!\nCluck... cluck... cluck.\"\nThe chicken looks up at you and then starts to scratch its claws into the ground. You think it is spelling out a word, but you are not sure what it is. Could it be... S-A-L-D-E-A-N? Before you can ask, the chicken turns away and goes about its business.","back":"The chicken stares at you with dark, cold eyes. It waits for you hungrily.\n\"BACAAAW!\nCluck...cluck...cluck.\"","done":"\"BACAW!!!\"\nThe chicken starts to gobble up the feed you put down.\nAfter a moment, the chicken looks around, startled. It uncomfortably shuffles back and forth. Is this chicken pregnant? You think you better check underneath it.\nWestfall Elwynn Forest The Barrens Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":38.2,"y":57.1,"n":"Chicken","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":36,"y":60.1,"n":"Chicken","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":60.8,"y":55.5,"n":"Chicken","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1061":{"id":1061,"t":"The Spirits of Stonetalon","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Seereth Stonebreak in the Stonetalon Mountains.","desc":"The spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains are angered, for goblins and their servants are plundering and burning the land. So the land has cried out, and those who listen for such things... have heard.\nSeereth Stonebreak, a promising shaman of the Horde, was sent to Stonetalon. She reports massive deforestation at the hands of the goblins, and requests aid.\nMeet Seereth in Stonetalon. To reach her, follow the road west of the Barrens' Crossroads. She is camped near the Greatwood Vale.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Ah, a ‹class›. Very good. We will need your skills to deal with these plunderers!\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Zor Lonetree","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.3,"y":27.9,"n":"Seereth Stonebreak","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6421":{"id":6421,"t":"Boulderslide Ravine","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Explore deep into the cave at Boulderslide Ravine and bring back 10 Resonite Crystals for Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat to investigate.\n10 Resonite Crystal Resonite Crystal , Resonite Crystal , Resonite Crystal , Gogger Stonepounder 80 % and 2 more","desc":"Something is amiss here in Stonetalon. Can you feel the tension in the air, ‹name›?\nSoutheast of here lies a deep cave in Boulderslide Ravine. The kobolds there are frantically mining a rare crystal called Resonite. I need you to bring back some ore samples so that I can understand what's happening in that cave. I also need you to investigate the depth of that cave.\nGo young ‹class›, it's imperative I know what evil lurks under these mountains.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"What news have you discovered from Boulderslide Ravine? I recall some legend that deals with Resonite... I just cannot place my hoof on it. Perhaps knowing what lies at the bottom of the cave will illuminate their devious intentions.","done":"Ah... Yes! That's it; the Resonite crystals have a trace of Earthen magic. The Kobolds must have dug deep uncovering an Earthen.\nLegend states that the Earthen are creatures created by the Titans. They were used to create the land our feet walk on. This most definitely is a threat that cannot be ignored.\n<Mor'rogal shakes his head.>\nPerhaps I can enchant these ore samples to use against this Kobold plot.\nStonetalon Mountains Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":64,"n":"Mor'rogal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1301":{"id":1301,"t":"James Hyal","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Vincent Hyal in Menethil Harbor.","desc":"Before working here at the Blue Recluse, I was trained by one of the best chefs and innkeepers I'd ever met. His name was James Hyal. Everything I have and everywhere I've gotten in life is thanks to him.\nI wonder how he's doing. His brother Vincent and he went to work in a tavern in Menethil Harbor, but I haven't heard from him recently.\nIf you ever happen to be headed in that direction, maybe you could say hello to him for me?","rew":"Experience: 700","done":"James? Oh, he left quite some time ago.\nFelt the second wind of patriotism, I suppose. Not hard to see why he would. With all the insanity in Lordaeron, many people joined up with Jaina Proudmoore when she went across the sea.\nStormwind City Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.1,"y":95.5,"n":"Connor Rivers","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.4,"y":61.8,"n":"Vincent Hyal","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"6501":{"id":6501,"t":"The Dragon's Eye","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You must search the world for a being capable of restoring the power to the Fragment of the Dragon's Eye. The only information you possess about such a being is that they exist.\nFragment of the Dragon's Eye\nProvided: Fragment of the Dragon's Eye","desc":"A fragment of the shattered medallion is all that I can offer.\nYou must find another of dragon blood willing to assist you in forging a new key. Once you secure this key, you must travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh. It is there that you will find her lair, ‹name›.\nWhere to find other flights willing to help? Sadly, I do not know... They are said to exist. Some may even work and live among us, disguised as one of the humanoid races. I wish you luck.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"I sense an aura of evil radiating from you, ‹race›. What could you hold that emits such an aura?","done":"I should have known - a piece of the black dragon brood mother, Onyxia. How revolting...\nStormwind City Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":54.5,"y":51.2,"n":"Haleh","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7781":{"id":7781,"t":"The Lord of Blackrock","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Head of Nefarian to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind.\nHead of Nefarian Nefarian\nProvided: Head of Nefarian","desc":"The old feeling returns. The welcome pangs of victory reverberate throughout your being. Before you lies the monolithic, battle scarred head of Nefarian. Return it to your Highlord, champion.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind\n+200 reputation with Ironforge\n+200 reputation with Darnassus\n+200 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Inconceivable!","done":"You need not be told the meaning of what you have done, ‹name›. This day will be recorded in the annals of history. A victory the likes of which has not been known to the Alliance for years - if ever!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"581":{"id":581,"t":"Hunt for Yenniku","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 9 Bloodscalp Tusks to Nimboya at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\n9 Bloodscalp Tusk Bloodscalp Scavenger 37 % , Bloodscalp Mystic 37 % , Bloodscalp Beastmaster 37 % , Bloodscalp Shaman 37 % and 4 more","desc":"A doom, there is. A doom on my chief's youngest son, Yenniku. As is a custom with our people, he was given to the Gurubashi Trolls of Zul'Gurub, but after my tribe, the Darkspear tribe, left with the orc Thrall, poor Yenniku was lost to us. I was sent from distant Orgrimmar, back to Stranglethorn, to search for my chief's son.\nAnd I believe the Bloodscalp tribe has him.\nIf you would help me, then hunt the Bloodscalps. You may find them to the north. Gather their tusks and return to me.","rew":"Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹class›. Show me you have made prey of the Bloodscalp tribe.\nShow me your trophies.","done":"These are good tusks, ‹name›. You prove that you have the strength to hunt the Bloodscalps.\nAnd that is good, because you are not done hunting them.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"341":{"id":341,"t":"Chapter III","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring pages 18, 20, 21 and 24 of Nesingwary's The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to Barnil Stonepot in order to complete Chapter III.\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 18 Verifonix 6.7 % , Bookie Herod 2.6 % , Mok'rash 2.5 % , Sergeant Malthus 1.9 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 20 Mosh'Ogg Butcher 4.7 % , Roloch 1.8 % , Lord Sakrasis 1.5 % , Negolash 1.4 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 21 Verifonix 1.6 % , Bookie Herod 1.6 % , Murkgill Oracle 1.3 % , Sergeant Malthus 1.3 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 24 Roloch 2.7 % , Captain Stillwater 1.3 % , Bookie Herod 1.2 % , Saltscale Tide Lord 1.2 % and 4 more","desc":"Chapter III was my favorite. It tells of Sir Erlgadin and Lady Rouack's first kill with a dwarven rifle. And the end of Chapter III, why, such a cliffhanger!\nLooks to me as though we still need pages 18, 20, 21 and 24 to finish the chapter. Those pages are out there somewhere. . .","rew":"You will receive:\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter III\nExperience: 775","back":"Any luck with pages 18, 20, 21 or 24? Those are the only ones we need to piece together Chapter III.","done":"Phew! Good work, ‹name›. Chapter III is now back together in one piece!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8181":{"id":8181,"t":"Confront Yeh'kinya","lv":58,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yeh'kinya.","desc":"My delvings into the Mosh'aru Tablets bear grim news, ‹name›. Hakkar's true form, the god himself, can be born again through the very egg into which you captured him. Yeh'kinya told you it was to contain his evil, but it is to recreate it! The troll has led you astray!\nGo to Yeh'kinya and demand the egg from him. Pray that it is not too late to stop Hakkar's return!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFaded Hakkari Cloak Tattered Hakkari Cape\nExperience: 6,200","done":"So, you have been speaking with that old dwarf Ironboot and uncovered the lost Mosh'aru Tablets, have you? That meddling prospector...\nNo matter. It is too late to save this world. Hakkar has been reborn, and even now grows in power... deep in the ancient troll kingdom of Zul'Gurub! He has come! And he will rule in blood and terror!\nThank you, ‹name›. Your help has sped the return of the Soulflayer!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.9,"y":24,"n":"Prospector Ironboot","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":22.4,"n":"Yeh'kinya","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2741":{"id":2741,"t":"The Super Egg-O-Matic","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 47 instead of 60.","obj":"Hippogryph Egg Hippogryph Egg","rew":"You will receive:\nEgg Crate\nExperience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Super Egg-O-Matic is the latest of Curgle Cranklehop's inventions. It is quite an impressive piece of machinery.\nThe Super Egg-O-Matic sputters wildly as you approach the control panel.","done":"You place the hippogryph egg into the machine. A series of beeps follows along with some strange mechanical sounds.\nIt appears that the Eggometer has weighed, measured, and packaged your egg. Now that's speedy service!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":27,"n":"Egg-O-Matic","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2661":{"id":2661,"t":"Delivery for Marin","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sprinkle wants to you take the Violet Powder to Marin Noggenfogger in Gadgetzan.\nViolet Powder\nProvided: Violet Powder","desc":"Here's the Violet Powder, ‹name›. Take it to Marin and tell him he owes me a favor!","rew":"Experience: 460\n+25 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Oh, ‹name›, you're finally back. What have you brought?","done":"Violet Powder, eh? Let's give it a try -- it sure couldn't make it any worse, that's for sure!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.1,"y":26.9,"n":"Sprinkle","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":28.7,"n":"Marin Noggenfogger","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"901":{"id":901,"t":"Samophlange","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Console Key from Tinkerer Sniggles to use on the control console.\nConsole Key Tinkerer Sniggles","desc":"With the apparatus deactivated, the control panel can be opened up and the samophlange removed from the console. With everything else in place, all that is left is to acquire the key to unlock the console.","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","back":"The console lights are dimmed and the gauges and dials all read at their zero positions, everything idling.","done":"Turning the key in the lock, the control console unlocks. A red light at the top of the console turns off and all power drains from the terminal.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.4,"y":11.6,"n":"Control Console","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"821":{"id":821,"t":"Chen's Empty Keg","lv":15,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Savannah Lion Tusks, 5 Plainstrider Kidneys, and 1 Thunder Lizard Horn to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.\n5 Savannah Lion Tusk Savannah Patriarch 55 % , Savannah Highmane 55 % , Savannah Huntress 55 % , Savannah Matriarch 55 % and 3 more\n5 Plainstrider Kidney Greater Plainstrider 40 % , Ornery Plainstrider 40 % , Fleeting Plainstrider 40 %\nThunder Lizard Horn Stormhide 20 % , Thunderhead 20 % , Stormsnout 20 % , Owatanka 20 %","desc":"Would you like a taste of Chen's namesake? Ahh, the stormstout is a mighty brew. Chen taught the recipe to my mentor, and my mentor passed it on to me. I'll need you to get me a few things, but I can tell you this: the kick is worth it.\nBring me 5 savannah lion tusks from any savannah lion, 5 plainstrider kidneys from any plainstrider, and 1 thunder lizard horn from any species of thunder lizard. That should do the trick nicely.\nYou can find these ingredients throughout the Barrens.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Stormstout\nExperience: 1,350\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How's the search going?","done":"Haha... I never thought I'd make more of this stuff ever again.\nYou've stirred in me a great sense of nostalgia, ‹name›. Kind of reminds me of the last time I blacked out from too much trogg ale. Thank you. The memories warm my stomach.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":38.4,"n":"Brewmaster Drohn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3301":{"id":3301,"t":"Mura Runetotem","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mura Runetotem in the Sepulcher.\nSample Snapjaw Shell\nProvided: Sample Snapjaw Shell","desc":"My clanmate, Mura Runetotem, traveled to Silverpine so that she might aid our undead allies. Silverpine is an ailing forest, a dying forest, and it was Mura's hope to bring it new life. Perhaps the strange life found here in the Barrens can help her work in Silverpine.\nTake a sample of the shells you gathered, and bring it to Mura in Silverpine. She is staying at the Sepulcher. With luck, studying the shell will give her the insight she needs to heal that dying place.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nJackseed Belt Sower's Cloak\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I can smell the dust of the Barrens on you, ‹class›. You have traveled far.","done":"Ah, what is this? This shell has an inner glow, as if it still pulses with life. Amazing! I must study it further.\nThank you, ‹name›. With luck, this shell will hold a secret I can use to aid the poor land of Silverpine.\nThe Barrens Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.9,"y":42,"n":"Mura Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"95621":{"id":95621,"t":"Trouble in the valley","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to the wrecked caravan and learn more about why the Kul Tirans are here.\nBenedict's Orders","desc":"This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras.\nIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.","back":"The remnants of Daelin Proudmoore's fleet who still fly his banner are just as rotten and barbaric as the admiral himself was before he died.\nI don't know why they are so far from Tiragarde, but it can't be good.","done":"So they are looking for a deserter... Well, it seems that the past has finally caught up to me.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":42,"y":11.4,"n":"Walton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4021":{"id":4021,"t":"Counterattack!","lv":20,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Piece of Krom'zar's Banner to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.\nPiece of Krom'zar's Banner Krom'zar's Banner","desc":"The Horde commends your successes against the Kolkar, but the Kolkar themselves are maddened. I have reports that a contingent of Kolkar has traveled to the Barrens from their home in Desolace, to seek vengeance. My latest report was that, even now, they move against these bunkers, from the west!\nFace the Kolkar invaders, and end their threat in the Barrens. Kill them until their leader, Warlord Krom'zar, appears. Defeat him and bring me a piece of his banner as proof.\nWe're counting on you, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the banner?","done":"You have done it! You have defeated the Kolkar!\nI will be sure Thrall receives word of your actions here, ‹name›.\nStand tall. You do yourself, and the Horde, proud.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7861":{"id":7861,"t":"Wanted: Vile Priestess Hexx and Her Minions","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You have been ordered to slay Vile Priestess Hexx and 20 Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guards. See Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands once this task is complete.\nVile Priestess Hexx and the Aman'zasi Guards can be found atop Jintha'alor in the Hinterlands.\nVile Priestess Hexx slain\nVilebranch Aman'zasi Guard slain : 0/ 20","desc":"By order of Primal Torntusk, Vile Priestess Hexx and her minions are to be brought to justice!\nA grand reward is offered for any that slay the Vile Priestess Hexx and all of her Aman'zasi elite guard.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWoven Ivy Necklace Deep Woodlands Cloak\nMoney: 2 25 2 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,100\n+200 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Do you bring news from Jintha'alor?","done":"A crippling blow to the Vilebranch, indeed. You shall be richly rewarded, ‹name›.\nThe Hinterlands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.1,"y":79,"n":"Call to Arms!","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Primal Torntusk","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"4821":{"id":4821,"t":"Alien Egg","lv":26,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Alien Egg to Hagar Lightninghoof in Freewind Post.\nAlien Egg Alien Egg","desc":"A rumor has surfaced about an alien egg here in Thousand Needles. Those that report seeing this egg have failed to even get close enough to examine it in detail. Serpents guard the egg as if it's one of their own.\nI want you to seek out this alien egg and bring it to me so that I may examine it. Reports say the egg is located within a serpent den, but there are several serpent dens along the base of the cliff walls south and northeast of Freewind Post.","rew":"Money: 15 0 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I must know more about this mysterious egg, who knows what will hatch from it.","done":"Yes, finally... the mysterious egg has finally been delivered to me. Now, let me take a closer look at this... What..! What is this..?","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":44.6,"y":50.3,"n":"Hagar Lightninghoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"99141":{"id":99141,"t":"Patience","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Obtain reports from Deathguard Dillinger, Deathguard Kristof, and Gordo for Executor Zygand.\nDillinger's Report\nKristof's Report\nGordo's Report","desc":"Make no mistake, ‹class›--the Dark Lady demands the perfect execution of her will. As an Executor, it is my duty to see that this happens.\nReports from several of my Deathguards are overdue. Needless to say, my patience has run out. Obtain their reports and bring them to me in the Dark Lady's name.\nYou will find Deathguard Dillinger just west of here, by the graveyard. Deathguard Kristof is stationed at the waystation to the east. And check on the abomination Gordo; he wanders west near Stillwater Pond.","back":"You'd best have those reports in hand, or get out of my face.","done":"I should have known better than to think an abomination could write anything of use. Let us keep that lapse of judgment between us.\nYou have pleased me, and therefore pleased the Dark Lady. Perhaps there is hope for you.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2341":{"id":2341,"t":"Necklace Recovery, Take 3","lv":44,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 37 instead of 40.","obj":"Visit Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath to see if he was successful.","desc":"As Dran and Malton Droffers begin to squabble over their new salvage, half of the deal is now complete. A trip to the Badlands is now in order to finish things up, as Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath might have a special reward waiting for you there.","rew":"You will receive:\nJarkal's Enhancing Necklace\nExperience: 5,600\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"The power source you gave me exceeded every expectation I had for it. I was able to make both you and me a necklace, and I have enough left over to make at least three more. They will fetch quite the fee, with Droffers and Son Salvage none the wiser.\nHere you go, my friend. I give you my thanks on a splendid job... and something quite special for your trouble.\nOrgrimmar Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3941":{"id":3941,"t":"A Gnome's Assistance","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find J.D. Collie in the cave at Marshal's Refuge.","desc":"Thinking... Thinking... I know I came here for something important...\nI have an idea, ‹name›. In the cave over there is a gnome named J.D. that was very kind to me when I first arrived here. Perhaps in my disoriented state, I might have mentioned something to her.\nWhy don't you go ask her if she knows anything? Oh, but be careful -- she's always messing with those crazy glowing crystals I've seen in the crater. I'm not quite sure what she's up to in there!","rew":"Experience: 1,250","done":"Stay where you are for just a moment... I am testing out a new combination of crystals...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4501":{"id":4501,"t":"Beware of Pterrordax","lv":55,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Pterrordax and 15 Frenzied Pterrordax, then speak to Spraggle Frock at Marshal's Refuge.\nPterrordax slain : 0/ 10\nFrenzied Pterrordax slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Wanted: A skilled fighter to deal with the threat of the Pterrordax that inhabit the Un'Goro Crater. Their numbers are growing, and they are becoming a menace to travelers in the area.\nDecrease the population by slaying 10 pterrordax and 15 frenzied pterrordax.\nSpeak with Spraggle Frock after completing the task for a reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrotslab Gloves Cragplate Greaves\nExperience: 5,650","back":"To tell you the truth, I really wasn't that worried about the strange creatures... Until the day that I saw it written on the side of a large stone.\nBEWARE OF PTERRORDAX\nWho could have written it? I don't know, but it's too creepy to just ignore!","done":"I am absolutely terrified of the pterrordax here! Thank you for decreasing their numbers, ‹name›. Now I might feel safe enough to venture out of Marshal's Refuge.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.5,"y":8.4,"n":"Beware of Pterrordax","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.6,"y":8.5,"n":"Spraggle Frock","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4661":{"id":4661,"t":"Testing for Corruption - Felwood","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Felwood Slime Sample Tainted Ooze , Cursed Ooze , The Ongar","rew":"You will receive:\nCorrupt Tested Sample","back":"You take a sample of slime from Felwood and place some of it into the various tubes and beakers on the table. As things begin to boil and spurt, the slime changes colors. When the process slows down and the liquids calm, you see a small petri dish with your altered Felwood slime samples in it along with some other remnants.","done":"You pick up the petri dish with the slime sample in it. The only way to discern if the samples is pure enough is to open it and examine the contents yourself. Ideally you'll find a sample that fits Chemist Fuely's criteria.\nDun Morogh Undercity Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.2,"y":24.9,"n":"Testing Equipment","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":47.8,"y":73.5,"n":"Testing Equipment","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"6981":{"id":6981,"t":"The Glowing Shard","lv":26,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,150 experience instead of 2,650, 1.94 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.\nThen, deliver the shard as you are directed.\nGlowing Shard Mutanus the Devourer\nProvided: Glowing Shard","desc":"The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.\nMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.","rew":"Experience: 5,150","back":"Hello, ‹race›. What can I do for you?","done":"Oh... I have never seen anything like this...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.2,"y":32.8,"n":"Falla Sagewind","e":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"8421":{"id":8421,"t":"The Wrong Stuff","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Rotting Wood and 4 Bloodvenom Essence to Impsy in Felwood.\n10 Rotting Wood Withered Protector 26 % , Irontree Stomper 25 % , Irontree Wanderer 25 %\n4 Bloodvenom Essence Tainted Ooze 20 %","desc":"Now that I have my felcloth, I can really begin making *my* pet.\nIt's going to need some eyes though. Perhaps you could rip some rotting wood from the irontree folk for me, so I can carve out some lovely eyes. They're up north in the Irontree Woods.\nI'll also need some bloodvenom essence to give it that new demon smell. The tainted oozes carry the essence, and they hang out right here near Niby and me.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Do you have the goods?","done":"This will work so very well.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1701":{"id":1701,"t":"Fire Hardened Mail","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather the materials Furen Longbeard requires, and bring them to him in Stormwind.\n50 Scorched Spider Fang Cave Stalker , Leech Stalker\n12 Charred Horn Fledgling Chimaera 80 % , Young Chimaera 80 %\nGalvanized Horn Chimaera Matriarch 80 %\nVial of Phlogiston Roogug in Razorfen Kraul\nProvided: Furen's Instructions","desc":"So I gave you a nice shield, but we don't have to stop there. I know the secrets to make extremely hard mail armor. It's not easy and it takes very rare materials, but if you're willing to do the legwork then I'll make a piece for you.\nWhat do you say, ‹name›? If you're up for the challenge, then I'll give you a list of what to get and where to get them.","rew":"Experience: 2,300","back":"How goes the scavenger hunt, ‹name›? Do you have the materials?","done":"You got it all? Amazing! I was afraid those chimaeras would eat you up for sure!\nWell let's get started on that armor...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5221":{"id":5221,"t":"Dalson's Tears Cauldron","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arcane Quickener sold by Alchemist Arbington , sold by Apothecary Dithers\n5 Somatic Intensifier Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Foulmane 50 % , Jabbering Ghoul 50 % , Blighted Zombie 50 % and 4 more\n4 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.\nHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.","done":"Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":46.2,"y":51.9,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5861":{"id":5861,"t":"Find Myranda","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Uther's Tomb, located in the southern Plaguelands. Show Myranda the Hag Tirion's Gift.\nTirion's Gift\nProvided: Tirion's Gift","desc":"‹name›, you have done all that I have asked thus far. Only one step remains in your quest of redemption.\nYou must deliver the items you have collected to Taelan. Unfortunately, Taelan and his Scarlet Crusaders will attack you on sight.\nThere is only one way in which to deliver my message and that is through a guise of deception.\nTo the south you will find Uther's tomb. An old and trusted confidant of mine, Myranda, now resides there - seek her out. Show her the items and she will assist you.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"I knew this day would come.","done":"I was Tirion's most trusted advisor when he held rank as Lord of Mardenholde. I openly dissented the verdict passed by the Order of the Silver Hand and was banished for my insolence.\nHe has been through much heart ache and disappointment in his life, ‹race›. Are you prepared to right the wrongs set upon the Fordrings?\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":50.8,"y":77.8,"n":"Myranda the Hag","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5461":{"id":5461,"t":"The Human, Ras Frostwhisper","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Arathi Highlands, to the ruins of Stromgarde. Search Stromgarde for a Keepsake of Remembrance. If you find such an item, return with it to Magistrate Marduke.\nKeepsake of Remembrance Keepsake of Remembrance","desc":"The undead fear life just as the living fear death. It is not unusual for a sentient undead being to completely destroy all remnants of his or her previous life after having turned.\nUnfortunately, in order to create an artifact capable of reverting Ras Frostwhisper to a mortal, we must have a keepsake from his years among the living.\nYou must venture to the ruined city of Stromgarde, Frostwhisper's home, and search for such an item. May luck be with you, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"A keepsake of remembrance is a rare find, ‹name›.","done":"I had doubted the possibility of such an item existing. This certainly opens up an incredible opportunity - one we must not squander.\nPrepare yourself, ‹name›, for what I am about to ask of you will take you into the depths of hell.\nWestern Plaguelands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.6,"y":74.1,"n":"Magistrate Marduke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6181":{"id":6181,"t":"A Swift Message","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Lewis' Note to Thor the gryphon master.\nLewis' Note\nProvided: Lewis' Note","desc":"Although we don't get much aid from Stormwind directly, I do have a contact in the city who helps supply us with armor. His name is Osric Strang. His shop, Limited Immunity, is in the Old Town of Stormwind.\nOur supply of armor dwindles, and I must contact Osric for more. Can you take him this note?\nThe fastest way to Stormwind is through Thor, our gryphon master. He's just down the hill; bring him my note, and then take a gryphon to Stormwind.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You look like you're in a hurry. Well, then you came to the right place!","done":"You have to get this note to Stormwind? That's not a problem, you can take one of my gryphons!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":57,"y":47.2,"n":"Quartermaster Lewis","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Thor","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"6261":{"id":6261,"t":"Dungar Longdrink","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Osric's Crate to Dungar Longdrink the gryphon master.\nOsric's Crate\nProvided: Osric's Crate","desc":"‹name›, I gathered into this crate everything Lewis asked for. Can you take it to him?\nIf you've already spoken to Thor in Westfall, then you can take a gryphon back to him. Dungar Longdrink is our gryphon master, over in the trade district.\nSpeak with Dungar, then get this crate to Lewis as fast as you can. We don't want our fighting men and women in Westfall to go without fresh equipment!","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Is that sweat on your brow, lad? You've been running too much. Next time, take a gryphon!","done":"A crate for Westfall, eh? Have you been to Westall before? If so, then it's no problem, my friend. I have plenty of gryphons trained to fly that route!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.2,"y":61,"n":"Osric Strang","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":71,"y":72.5,"n":"Dungar Longdrink","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98021":{"id":98021,"t":"Journey to sentinel hill","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report To Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.","desc":"If you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, I'd recommend reporting to a man named Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall to the south, at the settlement known as Sentinel Hill. His people are in need of aid.\nAfter journeying here from another plane of existence, the problems our lands face may seem small. I assure you, the aid you provide to those impacted by such problems means everything to them, and you will grow stronger for your labors.\nGood luck out there, adventurer!","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+25 reputation with High Order","done":"I've been begging Stormwind for aid for months and he sends me a skinny elf? Well, beggars can't be choosers I suppose.\nWelcome to Westfall, ‹class›. Let's see if we can't put you to work.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78,"y":18,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.2,"y":47.6,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"4901":{"id":4901,"t":"Guardians of the Altar","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Ranshalla while she attempts to reactivate the Altar of Elune. Report your findings to Erelas Ambersky in Rut'theran Village.","desc":"At the very top of the ridge lies what I believe to be an altar of the goddess Elune. From what I can tell, we need to light the five torches in each cave, and then we will be able to access the altar directly.\nI transcribed some incantations carved into the stone in the ancient ruins of Kel'Theril, which I believe are the secret to unlocking the altar. I'll need your help to light each torch, while I recite the spell.\nIf we are successful, you'll be able to report our findings to Erelas!","rew":"Experience: 4,800\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Did you meet up with Ranshalla?\nWinterspring Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":63.1,"y":59.5,"n":"Ranshalla","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93461":{"id":93461,"t":"Welcome to shendar village","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Rathiril Sunlance and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.\nSpeak with Rathiril Sunlance\nSpeak with the Innkeeper","desc":"You've got that \"High Order\" look to you. Those with Highborne ancestry always seem to have a slight twinkle in their eyes that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident High Order elder Rathiril Sunlance. You can find him here in the main lodge, just around the corner from me.\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.","done":"Checked in with Rathiril then? Great. Lots of tension between the High Order and the Windshapers these days, but they keep things civil here in Shen'dar. Well, at least in the village anyway. What happens out in the wilds stays in the wilds.\nNow that that's done, you look like someone who might be looking for something to do with their hands. I've got a few things that need doing, if you are game for a bit of work?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94901":{"id":94901,"t":"Hopping helpers","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect $1oa Gustjumper frogs.","desc":"[PH] Collect frogs\nLevel 11 , requires level 8 Difficulty 8 9 14 17 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 94901","cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92741":{"id":92741,"t":"Unwelcome visitors","lv":13,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to Shadowgale Forest and collect 8 Shriekling Talons for Iaadaria Bitterwind in Valanaar.\n8 Shriekling Talons","desc":"The Shadowgale Forest is incredibly dangerous and is usually off limits to normal adventurers. In recent months there's been an explosion in the shriekling population and they've started to expand their territory outside the woods, which is a potential problem. I have an interest in the alchemical properties of shriekling talons, so a much-needed culling also presents an opportunity for scholarly gain.\nTravel to Shadowgale Forest and hunt the beasts. Bring me as many of their talons as you can.","back":"The High Order does not make it a habit to employ themselves as simple trappers and game wardens, but when performing a service such as this can lead to scholarly gain, we are happy to engage in acts of community service.","done":"That is quite the haul of talons you've brought me. I cannot wait to dig into this!\nThank you for your service to the High Order, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":79.6,"n":"Iaadaria Bitterwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8101":{"id":8101,"t":"The Pebble of Kajaro","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nPebble of Kajaro\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"NULL","done":"‹race›, the pebble held within the frame of this talisman comes from Mount Kajaro in the South Seas. Mount Kajaro is an area plagued by volatility - marked by violent and oftentimes magical volcanic eruptions.\nAs your bond with the trolls of Zandalar grows, so too shall the power of this pebble. Harness the power of the pebble to strike down our enemies. Be like the mountain: Quick, explosive, deadly...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});